#====================================================================
# DRAFT-x11-pkgconfig-triple — x11 后端 GUI 库对 pkg-config x11+xext+xrender
#   三件套的硬性依赖与 XShape 硬错误
# 触发事件: gtk2 2.24.33 HarmonyOS PC 适配(前置适配轮)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-x11-pkgconfig-triple
trigger_tool:           configure|pkg-config
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        \*\*\* libX11 not found|
                        \*\*\* libXext not found|
                        Shape extension not found, check your development headers|
                        Package 'xext', required by 'virtual:world', not found|
                        No package 'xrender' found|
                        \*\*\* X development libraries not found

severity:               2
category:               build-system, dependency, autotools, platform, x11
match_keywords:         x11, xext, xrender, XShape, XShapeCombineMask, XextFindDisplay,
                        gdktarget, GTK_PACKAGES_FOR_X, X_PACKAGES, libXext.so,
                        libx11, libxrender, AC_PATH_XTRA, x11 backend, gdk-x11

title:                  x11-backend GUI libraries hard-require the pkg-config x11+xext+xrender triple and fail on missing XShape even when every other extension is optional

root_cause: >
  GTK2-style x11 backends probe three pkg-config packages together
  (`$PKG_CONFIG --exists x11 xext xrender`); failure falls back to
  AC_PATH_XTRA native X detection, which cannot work in cross environments.
  Two Xext entry points are unconditional AC_MSG_ERROR checks
  (XShapeCombineMask for the Shape extension, XextFindDisplay sanity probe),
  while xrandr/xcursor/XFixes/XSync degrade silently. Packages therefore
  fail or pass on the presence of one single library — libxext — regardless
  of how many optional X features are disabled.
affected_scope: >
  Every x11-target GUI/porting package in this repo (gtk2 and successors,
  plus any autotools port reusing the GTK X probe block). Current registry
  state: libx11/libxrender/libxrandr/libxfixes have OHOS binaries, libxext
  has recipes (6.4.0.x, upstream libXext 1.3.6) but no published OHOS
  binary, libxcursor is unadapted (degrades silently).

verification_cmd: >
  pkg-config --exists x11 xext xrender && echo triple-ok;
  conan list "libxext/*" -r ohpcd;
  conan list "libxext/<ver>:*" -r ohpcd -p "os=OHOS"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           declare-triple-requiring-libxext-recipe
rec_description: >
  Declare x11+xext+xrender (plus fontconfig for the GTK2 x11 backend) as
  explicit requires so PkgConfigDeps generates the .pc files configure
  probes. Keep optional extensions (xcursor/xinerama/xkb/shm/xinput) on
  their degrade-or-disable paths to shrink the dep surface. When a dep has
  recipes but no OHOS binary (libxext today), rely on --build=missing to
  build it from its in-repo recipe on the device; if that build fails, fix
  the dependency in its own PR — never vendor or patch the dependency inside
  the consumer package.
rec_command: >
  conan create archives/g/gtk2/2.24.33 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build="gtk2/*" --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-requirements-declaration

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      non-x11-backend-or-source-port
fallback_description: >
  If the x11 stack is unavailable for a package, only a non-X backend or an
  explicit source port (e.g. GTK3's broadway) avoids the triple; there is no
  configure switch that removes the XShape hard requirement while keeping
  the x11 backend.
fallback_command:       ""
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          backend-selection

forbid_1_pattern:       --without-x|gdktarget!=x11.*when.*x11.*required
forbid_1_reason:        Dropping to a non-X backend silently produces a package that cannot serve the consumer that needs gdk-x11.
forbid_1_consequence:   Configure passes but the consumer's gtk+-x11 probe fails downstream.

forbid_2_pattern:       vendored?lib[Xx]ext|copy.*libXext.*into.*(consumer|package)
forbid_2_reason:        Dependency adaptations belong to their own issue/branch/PR (one-library-one-PR).
forbid_2_consequence:   Unreviewable cross-package diffs and duplicate SONAMEs.

forbid_3_pattern:       status.*built.*before.*libxext.*binary.*exists
forbid_3_reason:        Marking a package built while its mandatory dep has never produced a target binary misrepresents readiness.
forbid_3_consequence:   Downstream xsane unlock decisions built on a package that cannot link.

principles:             P016
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E348
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:        DRAFT-gtk2-legacy-frontend (gtk2 unblocks the xsane GTK2 story)

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-x11-pkgconfig-triple.md
last_updated:           2026-09-12
source_event:           archives/g/gtk2/2.24.33

authors:                codex
source_pr:
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  0
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.8
metrics_last_used:      2026-09-12
